body:
### Tested versions

4.3

### System information

win11

### Issue description

What **not** it supposed to:
the color should not be sync;
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/40cc04d5-bc29-4463-b117-feb59bfcb05c)
What is supposed to:
the color is not sync (intented)
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/186be47f-5413-4089-92c5-5ae9ea9970d5)

I want to use a different number in different shader instances to make them look different without changing the uniform parameter in the script.
I can do this via INSTANCE_ID in 3d, but not in 2d.
In Canvas, this INSTANCE_ID always seems to be 0.
As demonstrated above, the shader code is meant to make different shader instances to do a color-changing animation with a time offset by a unique number which is INSTANCE_ID;

Maybe this is not implemented in canvas shader, or intended?

### Steps to reproduce

use the shader code below, create multiple sprites, and make shader Material unique.
The Color of sprites is sync in the case, which means INSTANCE_ID is always the same.
```
shader_type canvas_item; 
varying flat float seed;
void vertex() {
	seed = fract(float(INSTANCE_ID) * 0.1 + TIME);
}

void fragment() {
	COLOR = vec4(seed, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0);
}
```


